<title>USA: BTG stake cut by Vinik group.</title>
<headline>BTG stake cut by Vinik group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by former Fidelity Magellan Fund manager Jeffrey Vinik said Tuesday it cut its stake in BTG Inc to 565,200 common shares, or 6.7 percent from 8.1 percent previously held.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include the sale of 135,000 common shares between January 24 and March 17 at prices ranging from $19.3227 to $22.8442 per share.</p>
<p>BTG, based in Vienna, Va., is a computer products and services firm.</p>
